# LZH - Compress a file in CrLZH format

```text
LZH [drive:]file [destination-drive:]
```

## Compress a file

```text
B0:LZH A:REPORT.TXT D:
```

This writes REPORT.TYT on D. Both drives use the current user area.
Omitting the destination sends output to the logged drive.

## Restore a copy

```text
B0:UNLZH D:REPORT.TYT C:
```

[UNLZH](UNLZH.HLP) gets the original name from the stream. For
compressed help topics use [SQ](SQ.HLP) or [CR](CR.HLP), which produce
the .HQP and .HZP types HELP recognizes.
